<!--
  My work: a read-back of the student's own answers, for review and for a PDF
  (the Course renders only its selected child, so printing from here prints
  just this page). The end of Part 2's conversation sends the student here
  (hs_dialogue_part2.chatpeg, `hs_course.selectedChild <- ...`).

  Each answer is a {{...}} state template, written to print what the student
  entered and nothing else:
    * isFilled(...) ? ... : "*Not answered yet.*"   An unanswered field shows
      a quiet placeholder. (Unanswered readings are "", [] or, before the
      block has loaded, undefined; isFilled is false for all three, and the
      guard keeps toMarkdownBullets from ever seeing a non-list.)
    * toMarkdownBullets([...])   Typed text goes through it, even a single
      answer, because it Markdown-escapes: Markdown here also renders $...$
      as math, so "$800 rent and $200 deposit" would otherwise print as a
      formula, and a student's * or # would turn into emphasis or a heading.
      Paragraphs (blank lines) are kept; a single line break joins the lines.
    * Choice values ARE the option text in this course, so a choice prints
      as itself; the student's own option ("own", or "other" for a written-in
      research question) prints the text they wrote.
    * TabularMCQ grids are shown as the grid itself (<Use ref=...>),
      re-rendered with the student's answers (same state; still editable, as
      everywhere else in the course). The exception is the eight-column
      discipline grid (hs_disc_matrix), which is too wide for a printed
      page and is read back as one list of checked disciplines per cause.
-->

<Vertical id="hs_my_work" title="My work">

<Markdown id="hs_mw_intro"><![CDATA[
## My work

Everything you have entered in this activity so far, in the order you did it. To keep a copy, use the button below and choose **Save as PDF** as the printer.
]]></Markdown>
